      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Confidence calibration",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Claude’s call that “confident” is defensible is well grounded: it cites age progressing correctly from the 1850 census, the same county, the same household head, the same surname, and a consistent Irish birthplace. That is corroboration from the 1850 record, not a single-source link, so the LLM is wrong to say none was cited. The rule the LLM applies (“confident” requires multiple independent sources) isn’t in the judge context. And this audit wasn’t testing pe_004’s tier anyway; the target was the missing Thomas-side link."
