      "comment": "The LLM treats “Pennsylvania” as a contradiction, but it comes from the research question’s framing, not a sourced tree fact. Claude made that distinction explicitly, and the tool accepted the link without flagging a core-identifier conflict, as it did in the Trier test where the tree did attest a birthplace. Ireland is also consistent with the 1850 census elsewhere in this project. So “confident” holds for a_008 and a_009: exact name, zero age gap, same county, household under the known father, and a 0.90 score. The a_010 → I2 link at “confident” (0.84, exact name, head of household) is also sound."
