      "comment": "The judge context says identity is settled: this is the same “deceased” persona already linked to I1 at “confident” via pe_005, and its death date and place match I1’s recorded death. All assertions from one persona share that identity, so carrying “confident” to a_011 and a_012 isn’t circular. The Pennsylvania birthplace comes from a secondary informant (the son-in-law), so it doesn’t cap the tier, and Claude correctly passed it to conflict-resolution. The low 0.24 score is explained as a blank-persona artifact, not a real mismatch."
